# Consumer A's generated closure. `tools/library/verify-rust-consumers.mjs`
# materializes all of these inside a scratch tree on every run; none of them is
# source, and none of them should ever be staged.
#
# They are ignored here rather than assumed absent because they used to be
# written into this directory directly. A `git add examples/` at that point
# would have added 126 MB of cargo build output and sixteen vendored crates to
# the index, and nothing in the tree would have objected.
#
# `Cargo.lock` is deliberately NOT in this list. It is the closure's pin: the
# one file both `pnpm rust:bootstrap` (which derives its locked registry fetch
# from it) and the consumer proof (which asserts `--locked` against it) agree
# on. Without it committed, every run resolves the third-party closure anew
# and the two sides have no shared identity to be reproducible *about*. See
# ADR-R10 in `docs/rust/DECISIONS.md`.

deps/
target/
vendor/
.cargo/
lib/
